  <static seed="204" source="Library/272/setStewart12_5/problem_10.pg">
    <statement><p>Find an equation of a plane through the point (1, -3, 3)
which is orthogonal to the line 
<me>x = 2  - 2t, \quad y = -3
+ 3t, \quad  z = -2 + 1t</me> in which the coefficient of 
<m>x</m> is -2.</p>
<p>Equation: <fillin characters="60" name="AnSwEr0001"/> = 0.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-2\mathopen{}\left(x-1\right)+3\mathopen{}\left(y-\left(-3\right)\right)+1\mathopen{}\left(z-3\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
